    "notes": "Diwali hamper regifting is something every kitty group laughs about right now. POV: the viewer is the host, so the twist is personal ('sabse pehla naam... aapka'). Every tag is shown on a chip so a muted viewer reads the game: your name (2025), Ruhi's name on Shruti's hamper, 4 names crossed out on Aditi's, then the oldest name is yours (2022). Claim before reveal: Ruhi proudly 'Ekdum naya!' then the tag. Endings tried: (1) bank idea, all hampers go in the middle as the Housie prize, nice but a new beat after the twist and no callback; (2) the host writes a new tag for Ruhi, needs the viewer to act, not possible in POV; (3) kept: Ruhi pushes the same hamper back at the camera with the opening line, Aditi deadpans 'Phir se.', loops into the start. Rewrite 1 cut 'Tina' (show-off reels flat) and swapped the hook from a doorbell entrance to the hamper in the lens, since entrances lost 6-7 in 10 in 3 s. Every shot holds at most 2 short lines so none runs near 4 s (the group-chat reels failed QA on a 5.4 s shot). On-screen words avoid 'POV' (audience rule); the chip says 'AAP HOST HO'."
